========================================================================
PART 3: MODIFICATION AND ATTRIBUTION NOTICE
========================================================================

This repository contains modified and extended software based on the NIST
ELAS3D finite-element elasticity code described in NISTIR 6269.

Major modifications and extensions in ELAS3D-XTAL include, but are not limited
to:

1. Extension to anisotropic polycrystalline elasticity with grain-wise
   crystallographic orientations.
2. Rodrigues-vector orientation input and stiffness-tensor rotation for cubic
   single crystals.
3. HDF5-based input/output for large microstructure, orientation, stress, and
   von Mises stress datasets.
4. OpenMP parallelization of assembly, matrix-free operations, PCG iterations,
   energy evaluation, and post-processing.
5. Preconditioned Conjugate Gradient solver updates, including 3 x 3
   block-Jacobi preconditioning.
6. Active-node masking for pore/void-only nodes to improve numerical
   conditioning in porous microstructures.
7. Full-field stress and von Mises stress export for visualization and
   downstream fatigue analysis.
8. Integration with MATLAB-based synthetic microstructure generation,
   XCT-derived pore processing, PRISMS-Plasticity export, and fatigue-life
   prediction workflows.

These modifications were developed by:

   Juyoung Jeong and Veera Sundararaghavan
   Department of Aerospace Engineering
   University of Michigan
   Ann Arbor, MI 48109, USA

Repository:

   https://github.com/jjeongGrp/multifidelity-fatigue

